# English catalogue for PathMaster.
#
# msgids are English source text, so this file is the *identity* catalogue:
# every msgstr repeats its msgid exactly, and the completeness gate enforces
# that. Editing the English here without editing the msgid constant in
# `pathmaster-core::msgids` is therefore a build failure, not a silent
# divergence — there is one English text, named in the code and repeated here.
#
# It ships so that both languages take the same path through wxTranslations
# rather than English riding the miss-returns-the-msgid fallback, and so that a
# new translation starts from one file to copy rather than from the source.
#
# Two rules in every catalogue are load-bearing, not style (ADR-0004):
#
#   * A mnemonic keeps its Latin letter. In languages not written in Latin it
#     goes in parentheses — "Файл(&F)", never "&Файл".
#   * A tab character never appears in a translation. Accelerators such as
#     Ctrl+Z are appended by the code; typing one here would delete the
#     shortcut rather than misread it.
#
# Named braces — {n}, {operation} — are placeholders and must survive
# translation exactly, name for name. Percent signs are data: %PATH% and
# %SystemRoot% are the values this application edits.
#
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: PathMaster 0.1.0\n"
"PO-Revision-Date: 2026-08-20 12:00+0300\n"
"Language-Team: English\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Language: en\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=2; plural=(n != 1);\n"

